  "player_text": "I walk up to the gate serjeant and ask what a lone traveler owes to pass, and whether the missing patrol changes who gets through.",
  "visible_motivation": "He is standing by the board with a roster, and the patrol warning is what has the gate on edge.",
  "intended_meaning": "I want the toll for one person and a straight answer on whether I can enter now.",
  "generation_attempt_1": "\"A lone traveler must present themselves at the gate and submit to the standard tolls and examinations,\" the gate serjeant explains, eyes flicking briefly toward the notice board. \"That hasn't changed, but with the patrol missing—the one usually passing through this choke—you'll find their usual route altered since the Ash Compact's census choke tightened.\"\n\nThey glance toward the northwest mud track past the stacked crates. \"The patrol took that path last, though we don't know their current fate. It doesn't change who may pass, but expect closer scrutiny and delays while replacements are marshaled.\"",
